@startuml Delete Trade Sequence

title Delete Trade - Kafka Async Flow

actor Client
participant "FastAPI\nEndpoint" as API
queue "Kafka\nBroker" as Kafka
participant "Kafka\nConsumer" as Consumer
participant "TradeService" as Service
participant "PostgreSQL" as DB

Client -> API: DELETE /trades/{id}/{version}
activate API

API -> API: Build Message\n{operation: "DELETE",\ndata: {trade_id, version}}

API -> Kafka: produce(topic="trades",\nkey=trade_id,\nvalue=message)
activate Kafka

Kafka --> API: Message Queued
deactivate Kafka

API --> Client: 202 Accepted\n{status: "accepted",\nmessage: "delete queued"}
deactivate API

== Async Processing ==

Kafka -> Consumer: poll() - fetch message
activate Consumer

Consumer -> Consumer: Parse JSON\nExtract operation="DELETE"

Consumer -> Service: delete_trade(trade_id, version)
activate Service

Service -> DB: get_trade(trade_id, version)
activate DB
DB --> Service: existing_trade or None
deactivate DB

alt Trade Not Found
    Service --> Consumer: HTTPException(404)
    Consumer -> Consumer: Log Error\n(Trade not found)
    Consumer --> Kafka: Skip Commit
else Trade Found
    Service -> DB: delete(existing_trade)
    activate DB
    DB --> Service: Success
    deactivate DB
    
    Service --> Consumer: True
    deactivate Service
    
    Consumer -> Consumer: Log Success
    Consumer -> Kafka: commit(offset)
    activate Kafka
    Kafka --> Consumer: Offset Committed
    deactivate Kafka
end

deactivate Consumer

note right of Consumer
  **Delete Processing:**
  - Removes trade from database
  - Trade must exist
  - Idempotent (same msg twice\n  → second fails gracefully)
end note

note right of Kafka
  **Ordering Guarantee:**
  All operations for same trade_id
  go to same partition, ensuring
  operations are processed in order
end note

@enduml
